(3) => the '<=6 coprime-to-30030 core' is NOT forced by DC (found families with 11-12 coprime).
    The UNIVERSAL invariant: coprime core <= 13 - (#runners needed to cover {2..14}) <= 12,
    a <=12-speed family, so LRC(<=13) gives it reach >= 1/13 > 1/14 REGARDLESS of size.

(4) is the '<=6 core' a BOUNDED-DIAMETER artifact? max #coprime-to-30030 over SMALL-diameter DC:
    Vmax<=25: max #coprime-to-30030 = 4  (e.g. [1, 3, 8, 11, 12, 13, 14, 17, 18, 19, 20, 23, 25])
    Vmax<=40: max #coprime-to-30030 = 5  (e.g. [14, 17, 19, 22, 23, 24, 26, 28, 30, 31, 36, 37, 39])
    Vmax<=80: max #coprime-to-30030 = 6  (e.g. [1, 7, 19, 23, 42, 44, 50, 53, 58, 65, 67, 72, 73])
    Vmax<=200: max #coprime-to-30030 = 7  (e.g. [8, 37, 68, 70, 71, 72, 89, 143, 151, 159, 163, 167, 191])
    => if max grows with Vmax, the '<=6' is a small-diameter artifact; the primes-heavy large-diameter
       families (A,B above) reach 11-12 -- the core SIZE is unbounded, but always <=12 (LRC-protected).
